Now we need to have origin_node_ready true (we will activate before loading). After load, origin_node_occupied true, origin_node_ready stays true (since we activated earlier). After unload, origin_node_ready remains true (unchanged). Good.

Now we need destination_node_ready true (init true). Destination_node_occupied true (init true). Good.

Now we need transport_leg_available true (init true). After we assemble leg, it becomes not available.

Now we need transport_leg_loading_authorized: need to call authorize_transport_leg_loading after leg assembled and origin_availability_locked true and candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (we will have). So after leg assembled and origin_availability_locked true, we can authorize.

Now we need to load container beta onto leg: load_container_onto_leg requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta, candidate_transport_leg_linked shift_candidate_beta transport_leg_alpha, candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta, loading_container_available loading_container_beta, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not loading_container_loaded loading_container_beta. We'll have all after previous steps.

Now after loading container, we have loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked true.

Now we need candidate_staged_for_loading shift_candidate_beta: stage_schedule_candidate requires candidate_prepared, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_loaded, loading_container_leg_linked, candidate_task_profile_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not candidate_staged_for_loading. We'll have all except need to ensure origin_leg_loaded false (we will avoid setting it). Good.

Now we need candidate_loading_verified shift_candidate_beta: use verify_loading_profile_nominal (requires candidate_staged_for_loading, candidate_skill_certificate_linked, candidate_operator_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_loading_verified). We'll have all except need to ensure destination_leg_loaded false (we avoid actions that set it). Good.

Now we need candidate_clearance_established shift_candidate_beta: use establish_clearance_nominal (requires candidate_loading_verified, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_clearance_established). We'll have all.

Now we need candidate_finalized shift_candidate_beta: we can do finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation after compliance_validation_complete.

Thus we need to get compliance_validation_complete shift_candidate_beta via verify_compliance_certificate (requires operator_alignment_confirmed shift_candidate_beta, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_beta compliance_certificate_alpha, not compliance_validation_complete). We'll get operator_alignment_confirmed after confirm_operator_alignment (requires constraint_applied shift_candidate_beta, candidate_operator_linked shift_candidate_beta driver_operator_alpha, not operator_alignment_confirmed). We'll get constraint_applied via apply_operational_constraint (requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta, candidate_task_profile_linked shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha, operational_constraint_available operational_constraint_beta, candidate_operational_constraint_linked shift_candidate_beta operational_constraint_beta, not constraint_applied). We'll have candidate_prepared after confirm_candidate_preparedness, candidate_task_profile_linked after attach_task_profile, operational_constraint_available assumed true, candidate_operational_constraint_linked already true (init). So we can apply.

Now after constraint_applied, we can confirm operator alignment.

Then assign skill certificate (we can do before or after operator alignment; doesn't matter). But verify_compliance_certificate requires operator_alignment_confirmed and candidate_compliance_certificate_linked. So we need both.

Now assign compliance certificate: we need to release from alpha then assign to beta. Release requires candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha (true). After release, compliance_certificate_available true. Then assign to beta requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta and compliance_certificate_available.

Thus we need shift_candidate_beta prepared before we can assign compliance certificate. So we need to prepare shift_candidate_beta early (after vehicle allocation and task profile linking). Good.

Now we need to also ensure candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma (we will allocate vehicle).

Now we need to ensure dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_beta: we will allocate dispatch slot after shift_candidate_beta is dispatch_ready (which we get after finalize). Actually allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate requires dispatch_ready ?candidate. So we need shift_candidate_beta dispatch_ready true before allocating slot. However finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation sets dispatch_ready ?candidate as effect. So we can finalize first, then allocate slot, then execute dispatch.

Now we also need dispatch_allocated origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha. For those we need them dispatch_ready first (via mark_*_dispatch_ready). Then allocate slot, then execute dispatch.

Now we need to ensure after executing dispatch, the vehicle becomes available (goal wants vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha and vehicle_unit_beta). Good.

Now we also need dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha? Not in goal. After we execute dispatch for each candidate, the slot becomes available again. After three dispatches, it will be available (since each dispatch makes it available). However we allocated slot three times (each time consumes availability, then dispatch makes it available again). After third dispatch, slot will be available. Goal does not require slot availability, but it's okay.

Now we need to ensure we don't violate any negative preconditions (like not dispatched etc). We'll manage.

Now let's outline steps.

We'll need to track state changes.

Let's list all actions we will need, in order.

We'll start with initial state.

Step 1: Activate origin node (make origin_node_ready true). Action: activate_origin_node ?origin_availability_alpha ?origin_node_alpha ?route_task_profile_alpha.

Preconditions: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (true), candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (true), origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha (true), not origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha (true), not origin_node_occupied origin_node_alpha (true). Effect: origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha.

Step 2: Assign operator to origin_availability_alpha (for lock). Action: assign_operator_resource ?origin_availability_alpha ?driver_operator_alpha.

Precondition: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (true), operator_available driver_operator_alpha (true). Effect: candidate_operator_linked origin_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha, not operator_available driver_operator_alpha.

Now operator_available driver_operator_alpha becomes false.

Step 3: Load origin payload. Action: load_origin_payload ?origin_availability_alpha ?origin_node_alpha ?cargo_payload_alpha.

Preconditions: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (true), origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha (true), cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha (true), not origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha (currently false? Actually origin_availability_locked is false initially). So ok. Effect: origin_node_occupied origin_node_alpha true, origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha true, origin_payload_linked origin_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha true, cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha false.

Step 4: Unload origin payload. Action: unload_origin_payload ?origin_availability_alpha ?origin_node_alpha ?route_task_profile_alpha ?cargo_payload_alpha.

Preconditions: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (true), candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (true), origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha (true), origin_node_occupied origin_node_alpha (true), origin_payload_linked origin_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha (true), not origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha (currently false). Effect: origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha true (already true from step1, but setting again), origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha true, cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha true, not origin_payload_linked origin_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha false. Note: origin_availability_locked remains true (unchanged). So after step4 we have origin_node_occupied true, origin_node_ready true, origin_availability_locked true, origin_availability_confirmed true, cargo_available true.

Now we have origin availability ready for lock? Actually it's already locked and confirmed, good.

Now we need to assign operator to destination? Not needed for goal but may be needed for lock_destination_availability if we want to ensure dispatch_ready? Actually mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready requires destination_availability_locked and destination_availability_confirmed (both true initially) and transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized. So we don't need to assign operator to destination. However we might need operator linked for destination for something else? Not required.

Now we need to prepare shift_candidate_beta.

Step5: Allocate vehicle unit gamma to shift_candidate_beta. Action: allocate_vehicle_unit ?shift_candidate_beta ?vehicle_unit_gamma.

Preconditions: candidate_created shift_candidate_beta (true), not vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta (true), vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma (true). Effect: vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta true, candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma true, not vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma.

Now vehicle_unit_gamma becomes not available.

Step6: Attach task profile to shift_candidate_beta. Action: attach_task_profile ?shift_candidate_beta ?route_task_profile_alpha.

Preconditions: candidate_created shift_candidate_beta (true), vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta (now true), route_task_profile_available route_task_profile_alpha (true?